        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: The D.O.C., Charles Manson, Paul McCartney\n- Products: The D.O.C.'s second studio album, a Beatles song\n- Concepts: album naming reference, \"loud and dirty\" sound\n\nFacts:\n- Paul McCartney said he tried to create a sound \"as loud and dirty as possible\" for the Beatles song \"Helter Skelter.\"\n- Charles Manson developed an idea or interpretation centered on the Beatles song \"Helter Skelter.\"\n- The D.O.C.'s second studio album was titled as a reference to Charles Manson's idea of \"Helter Skelter.\"",
