        "original_id": "4e4867e0-0980-541f-80b5-8ac001da4f5a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: The D.O.C., Charles Manson, Paul McCartney\n- Groups: The Beatles\n- Works: Helter Skelter (album), \"Helter Skelter\" (song), The Beatles' self-titled double album (the White Album)\n- Concepts: Charles Manson's \"Helter Skelter\" prophecy\n\nFacts:\n- In 1968, the Beatles released the song \"Helter Skelter\" on their self-titled double album, often known as the White Album.\n- Paul McCartney developed \"Helter Skelter\" as an attempt to create a sound as loud and dirty as possible.\n- On January 23, 1996, The D.O.C. released Helter Skelter as his second studio album.\n- The D.O.C.'s album Helter Skelter takes its name from Charles Manson's idea that the Beatles' \"Helter Skelter\" prophesied the end of the world.",
